# Commands run by the launchd job com.hakios.demo (see com.hakios.demo.plist).
# TEST3 tester variant, with the 2026-10-26 fixes: the NFC kickstart is first, the Music import
# starts at +5 s (not +60) and is repaired in the same pass, and nothing waits 120 s -- the
# 215010 session's boots were 8-53 s long and none of the tail ever ran.
/redwood/bin/hello_dyn started by launchd
/redwood/bin/svc_test
/redwood/bin/surf_test
/bin/ps -A
/redwood/bin/mg_test
# the processors: how many, and -- once the system has settled -- whether they work at the same time
/redwood/bin/cpu_test
/redwood/bin/cpu_test 240 &
# where iOS sends its sound, once SpringBoard is up
/redwood/bin/sound_test springboard route &
# a tester's song into the Music library: 5 s, not 60. In the BACKGROUND: music_import goes on watching
# the library at +60, +180 and +420 s, and a foreground run held every later line back 7 minutes
# (TEST4: media_import, ssh and the Files steps never started). The repair and the ML3 look are
# near the end of this file, long after the row is in.
/redwood/bin/music_import --wait 5 /redwood/share/music/Тёмный_принц-Отвратительный_король.mp3 RDWD.mp3 &
# ... and into the Files app (On My iPhone) with its cover, and the cover into Photos
/redwood/bin/media_import --wait 5 --files /redwood/share/music/Тёмный_принц-Отвратительный_король.mp3 /redwood/share/music/Отвратительный_король.jpg --photos /redwood/share/music/Отвратительный_король.jpg &
# USB networking (USB networking; kernel vayu_usbnet=3 usb_handover=1 usbnet_delay=60, en2 by ~+62 s): OpenSSH from the prefix
# on port 22, root/mobile, key only, keys in /var/<user>/.ssh (the prefix's own homes are /var/jb/var/<user>: a test run
# refused the key with a home-relative AuthorizedKeysFile); and en2 into use at every boot: configd's own service,
# else DHCP (net_test ensure), then what configd has and a name resolved
/var/jb/usr/sbin/sshd -D -e -h /var/root/.ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key -o UsePAM=no -o PasswordAuthentication=no -o PermitRootLogin=prohibit-password -o AuthorizedKeysFile=/var/%u/.ssh/authorized_keys -o SetEnv=PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/var/jb/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/var/jb/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/var/jb/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/var/jb/usr/bin:/sbin:/var/jb/sbin:/bin:/var/jb/bin &
/redwood/bin/net_test ensure en2 20 waitaddr en2 240 waitdns 30 store State:/Network/(Service/.*/IPv4|Interface/en2/.*|Global/IPv4|Global/DNS) resolve example.com tcp 1.1.1.1 80 &
# Sileo (system-ru3 has the Procursus rootless prefix as /jb; init grafts it onto /var/jb): the preparation the
# bootstrap wants once per boot, after SpringBoard is up (as rc.jobs.jb; no network on vayu yet, so no apt-get update)
/redwood/bin/sound_test springboard
# iOS's first-boot data migrators, which our boot never ran (src/run_migrator.m, as mobile): live 2026-10-25
# LaunchServices knew no plug-in (Files' On My iPhone provider -2001) and Music's sort data was missing
/redwood/bin/ls_rebuild --check
/redwood/bin/run_migrator 00LaunchServicesMigrator SystemAppMigrator MediaLibrary
/redwood/bin/ls_rebuild --check
# F6: the database rebuild alone left LocalStorage's plug-in record without
# NSExtensionFileProviderDocumentGroup (TEST14: the appex's Info.plist has it, NSExtension.attributes
# says "(absent)", pkd=no). registerPlugin: is the per-bundle call that reads that Info.plist and
# stores the record; it is idempotent and creates nothing, and it runs before fileproviderd is asked.
/redwood/bin/ls_rebuild --plugins
# F6, next step if the record is still missing the group (repair=0 in the summary): the stores are a
# cache of the plists on disk, so a record that stays wrong survives every rebuild of it. --fresh moves
# them aside (renames, never deletes, .f6-backup) and the rebuild below reads the bundles again.
#/redwood/bin/ls_rebuild --fresh
/var/jb/bin/sh /var/jb/prep.sh
# nfcd for the NFC bridge (vayu_nfc_ios=2), once the prefix is there. TEST4 FACT: /bin/launchctl does not
# exist on this system image ("/bin/launchctl: No such file or directory", exit 127), so the first kickstart never ran.
/var/jb/bin/launchctl kickstart -p system/com.apple.nfcd
# Files' On My iPhone: the directories fileproviderd needs, the app groups, and the enable the toggle asks for.
# F5 (TEST13B): storage=nil before the enable is the normal state -- TEST10's first provider object said
# url:(null) and the same enable brought <GroupContainers>/.../File Provider Storage back, so R17's "do
# not ask" is what kept files=FAIL in TEST12/13. The pass enables, prints pkd=/mcm= (the two inputs of the
# daemon's storage URL, asked from this side) and recovers fileproviderd if the domain-creating call still
# aborts it. --restart=20 because that daemon was spawned at 04:07:42 and the appex reached
# LaunchServices/pkd at 04:07:47-51 (media_import at 04:07:44 still answered "NOT FOUND"), so the process
# serving the enable has a provider list older than the registry (R14); one restart gives it the completed
# one before anything creates a domain.
/var/jb/bin/sh /redwood/etc/fp-dirs.sh
/redwood/bin/fp_enable --trace --wait=30 --restart=20 --retry=45
/usr/bin/fileproviderctl domain list
# fileproviderd's log onto the console (it is in a file on the phone; owner15 had no ssh to fetch it)
/var/jb/bin/sh /redwood/etc/fp-log.sh
# GPU-B: LS has the LocalStorage plug-in but NSExtension (pkd) does not find it: what pkd finds per extension point
/redwood/bin/ls_rebuild --check
# R17: the state the daemon settled into, read without changing anything -- the same provider object the
# Files app's toggle would be answered from, and whether it has a document storage URL by then.
/redwood/bin/fp_enable --check
# the song's sort data and the ML3 look, long after its import
/redwood/bin/music_import --repair RDWD.mp3
/redwood/bin/music_import --ml3 RDWD.mp3
# what nfcd made of the bridge: after the INIT the hwspoof line must be in the kernel log
/var/jb/bin/sleep 5
/var/jb/bin/launchctl print system/com.apple.nfcd
